    "result_text": "The full suite is just the acceptance tests (AcceptanceBase and AuditLogCapture are support classes). BUILD SUCCESS with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the telephone-uniqueness rule for owner creation by adding one new, self-contained class:\n\n**`src/main/java/.../rest/advice/OwnerUniqueTelephoneAdvice.java`** \u2014 a `@ControllerAdvice` implementing `RequestBodyAdvice`, mirroring the existing `OwnerRequiredFieldsAdvice` pattern already in this package.\n\nHow it works:\n- `supports(...)` scopes it to the **create** endpoint only (`OwnerFieldsDto` body on the `addOwner` method), so owner updates that keep their own telephone are unaffected.\n- `afterBodyRead(...)` normalizes the incoming telephone (reusing `OwnerMapper.normalizeTelephone`, the same non-digit-stripping used when storing) and, if any existing owner has a matching normalized telephone, throws a `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n- An `@ExceptionHandler` returns **409 Conflict**. `@Order(HIGHEST_PRECEDENCE)` ensures this specific handler resolves ahead of the global `Exception` handler (which otherwise returns 500 \u2014 the reason for the initial failure).\n\nStructural-impact notes: no existing method or class was grown. The change is a single new file whose methods each have tiny `WMC_other` (only their small sibling methods), rather than editing the large `OwnerRestControllerV1` or the service layer, whose high surrounding complexity would have dominated the cost.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (`coreRejectsDuplicateTelephone`, `functionalityAllowsDistinctTelephone`) and the full suite pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
